                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#presheaves"} Presheaves
              %li
                %a{:href => "#sheaves"} Sheaves
              %li
                %a{:href => "#presentations"} Presentations
              %li
                %a{:href => "#presheaves_2"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  \-Presheaves
              %li
                %a{:href => "#sheaves_2"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  \-sheaves
              %li
                %a{:href => "#abelian_sheaf_cohomology_as_special_case_of_stackification"}
                  Abelian sheaf cohomology as special case of
                  = succeed "-stackification" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h1#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
            – often called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            – is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categorical
            analog of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            There is good
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
          %p
            Here we recall basic definitions and then concentrate on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} 1-categorical models
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} present
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-categories of ∞-stacks
          %p
            What we describe is effectively the old theory of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            seen in the new light of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %h1#plan Plan
          %p We proceed as follow.
          %ul
            %li
              %p As a preparation,
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    we recall 1-categorical
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
                %li
                  %p
                    and how a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
                    may equivalently be thought of as
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        a category
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometrically embedded
                        into that of presheaves
                    %li
                      %p
                        or equivalently as the
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
                        of presheaves at
                        = succeed "." do
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphisms"} local isomorphisms
            %li
              %p Then in the main part, after recalling
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    the definition of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                  %ul
                    %li
                      and the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
                      of
                      = succeed "-categories" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn ∞
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} 1-categorical models
              %p we give
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    the general definition of
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
                  %ul
                    %li
                      and their
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
                      by the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structure on simplicial presheaves
              %p and finally
              %ul
                %li
                  the definition of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
                  by
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+%28infinity%2C1%29-subcategory"} (∞,1)-geometric embedding
                %li
                  and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} 1-categorical model
                  of this by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
                  to the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %h1#sheaf_toposes Sheaf toposes
          %p
            It is helpful to briefly recall the story that we want to tell in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            context, because in the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            context it will be
            %strong literally the same
            with all notions such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
            etc suitably regarded in the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
          %h2#presheaves Presheaves
          %p
            Consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that we want to think as a category of “test spaces”. Classical choices would be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Op(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Let
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            be the category of sets. We write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PSh(C) := [C^{op}, Set] := Func(C^{op}, Set)
          %p
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+and+quantity"} very general spaces
            modeled on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as described at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
          %h2#sheaves Sheaves
          %p
            In fact, this is a bit too general for most purposes: the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
            may be very non-local in that they don’t respect the way test objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are supposed to glue together. The full subcategory on those presheaves that do respect some kind of gluing of test objects is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
              into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh(C) \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} PSh(C)
                    \\,.
          %p Recall that this means that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C) \hookrightarrow PSh(C)
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo :
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar {(\cdot)} : PSh(C) \to Sh(C)
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} left exact
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
          %p in other words that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C) \hookrightarrow PSh(C)
                is the inclusion of a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            %li
              %p
                with the special property that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                to the inclusion is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} left exact
                (i.e. preserves finite
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
          %p
            In view of our models for
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              is equivalent to the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local
              presheaves, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is the set of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphisms"} local isomorphisms
          %p
            Another useful kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embeddings"} geometric embeddings
            is that of the point:
          %p
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*}
            be the category with a single morphism (the identity on a single object). Then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh({*}) \simeq Sh({*}) \simeq Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x : Sh({*}) \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} Sh(C)
          %p
            are called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} points
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            has
            %em enough points
            if isomorphisms of sheaves can be tested on points
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f : A \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} B)\in Sh(C)
                  \\;\;
                  \\Leftrightarrow
                  \\;\;
                  \\forall x : (x^* f : x^* A \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} x^* B)
                  \\,.
          %p This is the situation we shall concentrate on here.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Diff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(Diff)
                has enough points, one for every
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %li
              %p
                The topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(Op(X))
                has enough points: one for every ordinary point of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            has enough points, we may characterize sheaves in yet another way, which is the one that directly suggests the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
            discussed below:
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(PSh(C))
              be the set of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"}> stalk
                  wise isomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
              of presheaves such that for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* f : x^* A \to x^* B
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              (of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              has
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              is equivalent to the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              of
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
            that we are going to describe is obtained from this description of sheaves by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                replacing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %li
              %p
                replacing
                = succeed "wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                of sets by
                = succeed "wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} weak homotopy equivalences
                of simplicial sets.
          %p
            So the model structures we shall encounter are plausible guesses. What is less trivial is that this plausible structure indeed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
            the fully general notion of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
          %p This fully general notion we introduce now.
          %h1#categories_and_their_presentation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-categories and their presentation
          %p
            An ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} category enriched
            over the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C0%29-category"} (∞,0)-category
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            which we think of as modeled by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            that is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          %p
            Recall that there is a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %mi SSet
                  %mtext -
                  %mi Cat
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N : SSet\text{-}Cat \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} SSet : |-|
          %p
            for
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched categories
            induced by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} cosimplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi SSet
                      %mo −
                      %mi Cat
                  %mo :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo −
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta_{SSet-Cat} : \Delta \to SSet-Cat
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched categories
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_category
              Definition (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-category)
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} category enriched
              over
              = succeed "-groupoids," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              all whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
              happen to be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            %p
              Given two
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{D}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Func(\mathbf{C}, \mathbf{D}) :=
                    |SSet(N(\mathbf{C}), N(\mathbf{D}))|
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is indeed itself an
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop 1.2.7.3
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat
              is that whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  objects are
                  = succeed "-categories;" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{D}
                  two
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  = succeed "-groupoid" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Cat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat(\mathbf{C}, \mathbf{D})
                  is the maximal
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
                  inside the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                  of maps between the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerves"} homotopy coherent nerves
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Cat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mi Core
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi SSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (\infty,1)Cat(\mathbf{C}, \mathbf{D})
                        \:=
                        Core( SSet(N(\mathbf{C}), N(\mathbf{D})) )
                        \\,.
          %p
            %strong Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Using the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
                embedding
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi const
                      %mo :
                      %mi Set
                      %mo ↪
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpdf
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi SSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const : Set \hookrightarrow \infty Grpdf \subset SSet
                every ordinary category is an
                = succeed "-category." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"}> ∞Grpd
                ) is the full
                %span.newWikiWord
                  SSet]-subcategory of [[SSet
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/SSet%5D-subcategory+of+%5B%5BSSet"} ?
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_homotopy_category Definition (homotopy category)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+groups"} simplicial connected components
              functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_0 : SSet \to Set
            %p is strong monoidal and hence induces a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H : (\infty,1)Cat \to Cat
                    \\,.
            %p
              The image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(\mathbf{C})
              of an
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(\mathbf{C})(x,y) = \pi_0(\mathbf{C}(x,y))
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of an (∞,1)-category
            %p
              Two
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{D}
              are
              %strong equivalent
              if they are isomorphic in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H((\infty,1)Cat)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi is
                    %mi equivalence
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi is
                    %mi isomorphism
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f : \mathbf{C} \to \mathbf{D} \;is equivalence)
                    \\;\;
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;
                    (H_{(\infty,1)Cat}(f) : \mathbf{C} \to \mathbf{D}
                    \\;
                    is isomorphism)
                    \\,.
          %h2#presentations Presentations
          %p
            It is often convenient to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} present
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} models
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_category_presented_by_a_model_category
              Definition (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-category presented by a model category)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presented
              by it is the full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^\circ \subset \mathbf{A}
              on objects that are both cofibrant and fibrant.
          %p
            %strong Remark
            The axioms of a simplicial model category ensure that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-simplicial sets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^\circ
            are indeed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, remark 3.1.8
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_
              Proposition (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"}> HTT, remark A.3.7.7
              )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model categories
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^\circ
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^\circ
              are equivalent precisely if there is a sequence of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{A}
                    \\stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                    \\stackrel{\to}{\leftarrow}
                    \\stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                    \\cdots
                    \\mathbf{B}
                    \\,.
          %h1#sheaf_toposes_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-Sheaf
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            There is now an obvious definition of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-presheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h2#presheaves_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-Presheaves
          %p
            Now we generalize the above from sheaves to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            also known as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_presheaves
              Definition (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-presheaves)
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PSh_\infty(C) := [C^{op}, \infty Grpd] =
                    Func( C^{op}, \infty Grpd )
                    \\,.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_models_for_presheaves_
              Proposition (models for
              = succeed "-presheaves)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 4.2.4.4
            %p
              see also
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 5.1.1.1
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structure on simplicial presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPSh(C)_{proj}
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (either the projective or the injective one) is equivalent to that of
              = succeed "-presheaves" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi inj
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (SPSh(C)_{proj})^{\circ}
                    \\simeq
                    (SPSh(C)_{inj})^{\circ}
                    \\simeq
                    PSh_\infty(C)
                    \\,.
          %h2#sheaves_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-sheaves
          %p
            There are
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
                (preserving finite
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
          %p
            Using this we obtain a definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
            of
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-subcategories"} reflective (∞,1)-subcategories
            by literally copying the 1-categorical definition.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_sheaves_
              Definition (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-sheaves) (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"}> HTT, def. 6.1.0.4
              )
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
              into an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh_\infty(C) \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} PSh_\infty(C)
                    \\,.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#proposition_models_for_reflective_subcategories
              Proposition (models for reflective
              = succeed "-subcategories)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %p
              Let the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
              be a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mo ∘
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}^\circ \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{A}^\circ
            %p
              is the inclusion of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-subcategory"} reflective (∞,1)-subcategory
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop A.3.7.4
              every combinatorial simplicial left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
              is given by a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              of cofibrations such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the fibrant objects of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
                  are precisely the fibrant objects in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
                  that are
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
              %li
                %p
                  the weak equivalences of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
                  are the
                  = succeed "-local" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
            %p
              Accordingly
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^\circ
              is the full
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^\circ
              on
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop 6.5.2.14
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 5.5.4.15
              this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-subcategory"} reflective (∞,1)-subcategory
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
          %p
            %strong Remark
            Notice that this does not yet say that the localization is
            %em left exact
            \.
          %p
            But this makes at least plausible that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            for an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
          %p That this is indeed the case is
          #SizeOfLeftCoset.num_lemma
            %h6#proposition_model_for_hypercomplete_sheaves_
              Proposition (model for hypercomplete
              = succeed "-sheaves)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 6.5.2.14
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                      %mrow
                        %mi l
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSh(C)^{l loc}_{proj}
              presents the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompleted version
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi hc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh^{hc}(C)
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                      %mi loc
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi hc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (SPSh(C)_{proj}^{loc})^\circ
                    \\simeq
                    Sh^{hc}(C)
                    \\,.
          %p
            %strong Remark
            See the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cohomology"} Čech cohomology
            for the role of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
          %h1#applications Applications
          %h2#abelian_sheaf_cohomology_as_special_case_of_stackification
            Abelian sheaf cohomology as special case of
            = succeed "-stackification" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            operation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo +
                  %mo →
                  %mi SimpAb
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N : Ch_+ \to SimpAb \subset \infty Grpd
          %p
            embeds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
            with values in non-negatively graded
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            are realized as special cases of models for
            = succeed "-stacks:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-stack." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              identifies with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
              corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} infinity-stack
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} (infinity,1)-topos
            %p More precisely, let
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                  be the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo =
                        %mi Op
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Op(X)
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Sh(X)
                  be a sheaf with values in abelian groups on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi n
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi SSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n A \in Sh(X,SSet)
                  be the image of the complex of sheaves
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[-n]
                  concentrated in degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  under the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              %li
                %p
                  write
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Sh(X)
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  sheaf in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
                  (the sheaf constant on the singleton set).
            %p
              Then degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with coefficients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is homotopy classes of maps from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi n
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Ho
                      %mrow
                        %mi SSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^n(X,A) \simeq Ho_{SSh(X)}(X, \mathbf{B}^n A)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The original proof was given in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"} BrownAHT
              in terms of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
              structure on locally Kan simplicial sheaves.
            %p
              The analogous arguments in terms of the full injective model structure were given by Jardine. See section 6 of his
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uwo.ca/~jardine/papers/Fields-01.pdf"} lecture notes
